   "source": [
    "# Quantum Speed Limit for GKP State Preparation\n",
    "\n",
    "The Mandelstam-Tamm bound sets a minimum time\n",
    "$$\n",
    "T_\\min = \\frac{\\Omega_B}{\\lVert H \\rVert}, \\qquad \\Omega_B = \\arccos|\\braket{\\psi_i | \\psi_f}|,\n",
    "$$\n",
    "for driving $\\ket{\\psi_i} \\to \\ket{\\psi_f}$ under any Hamiltonian with spectral-norm bound $\\lVert H \\rVert$, and this bound is saturated by the quantum brachistochrone construction. For preparing a GKP logical state from the vacuum, $\\Omega_B$ is set entirely by the overlap $\\braket{\\text{vac} | \\psi_L}$, which depends sharply on the finite-energy envelope $\\Delta$: narrower envelopes (higher effective squeezing) mean less overlap with vacuum, larger $\\theta_B$, and longer minimum preparation time. This notebook computes that dependence for each of the six cardinal GKP logical states.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "52ad69a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Imports\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "067b8da2",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
