   "id": "c2f10eaa",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## System parameters\n",
    "\n",
    "Square-lattice GKP code with lattice spacings $\\alpha = \\sqrt{\\pi/2}$ and $\\beta = i\\sqrt{\\pi/2}$, lattice-sum truncation ``gkp_cutoff``, and unit spectral-norm bound $\\lVert H \\rVert = \\omega$ on the driving Hamiltonian. The Fock truncation $n_{\\text{fock}}$ is chosen per envelope $\\Delta$ (more squeezing needs more levels); the heuristic below is conservative enough for the $\\Delta$ range considered here but should be revisited for very small $\\Delta$.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "id": "f79c7371",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stderr",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "An NVIDIA GPU may be present on this machine, but a CUDA-enabled jaxlib is not installed. Falling back to cpu.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "gkp_alpha = jnp.sqrt(jnp.pi / 2)\n",
    "gkp_beta = jnp.sqrt(jnp.pi / 2) * 1j\n",
    "gkp_cutoff = 10\n",
    "\n",
    "energy_bound = 1.0\n",
    "n_fock_min = 50\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "def fock_cutoff(delta: float) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Heuristic Fock truncation: grows with effective GKP squeezing.\"\"\"\n",
    "    squeezing_db = -10 * jnp.log10(delta**2)\n",
    "    return max(int(squeezing_db * 15), n_fock_min)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e75b2b47",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Bures angle vs GKP envelope\n",
    "\n",
    "For each envelope $\\Delta$ and each cardinal GKP state $\\ket{\\psi_L}$, compute the Bures angle\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\Omega_B(\\Delta) = \\arccos \\bigl| \\braket{\\mathrm{vac} | \\psi_L(\\Delta)} \\bigr|.\n",
    "$$\n",
    "We use the package's `gkp_states` to build $\\ket{0_L}$ and $\\ket{1_L}$, then form the other four cardinal states as Bloch-sphere superpositions. Each state is embedded in its own Hilbert space sized by ``fock_cutoff(delta)``, so vacuum has to be rebuilt at that dimension for the overlap to be well-defined.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "ad821922",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
