   "source": [
    "## Bures angle and minimum preparation time\n",
    "\n",
    "Left: the Bures angle $\\Omega_B$ between vacuum and each cardinal GKP state, as a function of effective squeezing in dB. Right: the corresponding minimum preparation time $T_\\min = \\Omega_B / \\lVert H \\rVert$ under unit energy bound. Since $\\ket{1_L}$ has exponentially small overlap with the vacuum, its curve sits near $\\Omega_B = \\pi/2$ across the full range and sets an effective ceiling; $\\ket{0_L}$ at low squeezing is closest to vacuum and is therefore the cheapest target.\n"
   ]
  },
